---
greeting: Ahmad Ahandani
---

I'm a software engineer, and I build things because I enjoy it. A piece of woodwork or a desktop app, it doesn't matter much. The idea doesn't have to be new, and it doesn't have to change the world. I like making something that wasn't there before and watching it work.

These days that mostly means applied AI. I build AI features that hold up with real users, like [Edyt](/posts/introducing-edyt), a writing assistant for Mac and Windows. And I build tools for working with coding agents, like [Ramulus](/posts/ramulus-a-git-app-for-when-your-agent-writes-the-code), a Git app for when the agent writes the code.
